WEBVTT

00:39.910 --> 00:41.290
You're...

00:48.210 --> 00:49.790
We meet again.

00:55.220 --> 00:56.800
You're not going to jump?

00:58.720 --> 00:59.890
What?!

01:08.110 --> 01:10.150
A Type L Fuego, huh?

01:11.070 --> 01:13.440
--Were you chosen?
--Huh?

01:14.070 --> 01:15.030
Go.

01:23.290 --> 01:27.330
You seem displeased.
Would you have preferred the GGP?

01:28.790 --> 01:31.380
Who are you?

01:32.050 --> 01:36.170
My name is Kiefer. I'm an ordinary terrorist.

01:36.260 --> 01:38.720
Who are you, Rin Ogata?

01:39.680 --> 01:43.600
You're the mysterious "RideBack girl"
who broke through the GGP net

01:43.680 --> 01:47.230
and made quick work of special police vehicles.

01:47.310 --> 01:51.810
It isn't like that. I just needed to help people.

01:51.900 --> 01:53.480
You're wrong.

01:54.360 --> 01:58.400
You're bound by no one when you're on the Fuego.

01:58.490 --> 02:02.830
You changed your goal amid the blessed light.

02:03.490 --> 02:06.120
How do you know about that?!

02:06.210 --> 02:08.790
Because I'm just like you.

02:15.670 --> 02:19.550
You're free now. Someone will come for you soon.

02:19.640 --> 02:21.590
Just relax until then.

04:28.180 --> 04:33.640
What began as a small war in
the corner of a continent some 10 years ago

04:35.230 --> 04:39.320
eventually changed the entire world order.

04:43.400 --> 04:48.950
Originally, the GGP was nothing
but a small-scale resistance force

04:49.030 --> 04:52.790
that opposed a superpower's
military rule over the world.

04:52.870 --> 04:56.920
The difference in strength was colossal.

05:00.550 --> 05:05.720
The Arizona Campaign was
the legendary battle that changed it all.

05:07.050 --> 05:12.140
The ICBM base was the symbol of
the superpower's worldwide control.

05:13.390 --> 05:18.900
This impregnable castle could even
withstand a nuclear retaliatory strike,

05:18.980 --> 05:23.110
yet the RideBack squad fostered by
the brilliant scientist Killy McCannon

05:23.190 --> 05:25.700
launched a surprise attack on it.

05:44.210 --> 05:47.800
Led by the young Romanov Cullenberg,

05:47.880 --> 05:50.590
the squad succeeded in neutralizing the base.

05:50.680 --> 05:56.140
After this victory, the GGP rose to
become an overwhelming presence.

05:56.230 --> 06:01.230
However, their attempt to rescue
the imprisoned Dr. Killy ended in failure

06:01.310 --> 06:05.150
and half of the RideBack
squad perished in battle.

06:05.240 --> 06:08.950
Later, multiple high-ranking
soldiers in the squad were punished

06:09.030 --> 06:11.820
for breaching squad regulations.

06:13.740 --> 06:16.830
As a result, despite being an historic victory,

06:16.910 --> 06:21.630
the story of this legendary
battle has never been made public.

06:22.710 --> 06:27.340
Tenshiro Okakura is club advisor
to the mysterious "RideBack girl"

06:27.420 --> 06:31.930
and GGP Commander Romanov Cullenberg
was his old war buddy.

06:32.890 --> 06:36.100
RideBacks connect them all...

06:38.310 --> 06:44.360
And the military RideBacks are
manufactured by the Hesner Company...

07:02.210 --> 07:06.210
We got the stuff. It's time to get the party ready.

07:06.300 --> 07:10.010
You're going to draw the GGP in and set them off?

07:10.090 --> 07:12.340
What if they suddenly start air-raiding?

07:12.430 --> 07:15.760
No worries. They'll come with
their tails wagging for their dear Goblin.

07:15.850 --> 07:19.430
He only wants the corpses of me and Kiefer.

07:19.520 --> 07:21.690
Yes, that's right.

07:21.770 --> 07:23.230
Uncuff him.

07:26.480 --> 07:30.360
He's in a big mansion
five kilometers southwest of here.

07:30.450 --> 07:32.490
You'll have to go on ahead.

07:32.570 --> 07:35.740
We have some guests to greet here first.

07:35.830 --> 07:39.910
For self-defense.
You could probably do fine without it, though.

07:42.250 --> 07:46.210
Target vehicle remains at
a standstill. No activity at all.

07:46.290 --> 07:48.960
Seal all routes within a 5-kilometer radius.

07:49.050 --> 07:51.590
Bravo Team, get behind the target.

07:52.380 --> 07:55.550
It appears to be an unused weather-monitoring station.

07:55.640 --> 07:57.640
Shall we commence an air-raid?

07:57.720 --> 08:01.810
Not yet. We're going to stir up the maggots first.

08:01.890 --> 08:02.940
Zero-one.

08:27.460 --> 08:29.170
We've lost contact with the infiltration team!

08:29.250 --> 08:34.550
Word from Bravo. Target was
lost moving north-northwest.

08:34.630 --> 08:38.180
Locate all buildings they might flee into!

08:38.260 --> 08:40.850
Regroup all remaining forces and prepare to move out!

08:40.930 --> 08:44.270
Guttorm! Use the RideBack squad to cut them off!

08:44.350 --> 08:45.520
Zero-one!

08:51.480 --> 08:54.720
Okakura's seminars are
on hold for the time being.

08:55.660 --> 08:57.450
It's nice to see you again.

09:02.750 --> 09:07.290
Who would've guessed that
the heroic Goblin was working here...

09:09.210 --> 09:14.220
I'd like to talk to you about
Rin Ogata and Tenshiro Okakura.

09:18.430 --> 09:23.220
It's true that she resisted
the police trying to save her brother.

09:23.310 --> 09:29.060
But she wouldn't have been
arrested if I hadn't given her a lift.

09:29.150 --> 09:31.440
I feel a little bit responsible.

09:31.520 --> 09:36.150
So, how does Okakura fit into this?

09:36.240 --> 09:39.990
GGP Commander Romanov Cullenberg.

09:40.990 --> 09:43.160
They were old war buddies.

09:43.250 --> 09:44.870
War buddies?

09:44.960 --> 09:49.460
From what I could find,
they didn't get along that well, though.

09:49.540 --> 09:51.630
In fact, it's possible he's being targeted.

09:52.590 --> 09:54.670
What do you want from me?

09:54.760 --> 09:56.840
We might be able to save Rin Ogata.

09:56.930 --> 10:00.550
I have the story, but I'm missing a piece of evidence.

10:00.640 --> 10:05.680
I need inside connections
to get it. Do you understand?

10:05.770 --> 10:07.020
Sure.

10:07.100 --> 10:10.690
But in exchange, you'll help me, too.

10:12.570 --> 10:14.710
Private property

10:12.570 --> 10:14.710
No trespassing

10:32.420 --> 10:34.000
B-Knights.

10:36.010 --> 10:39.510
They're the BMA's primary machines.
Want to try one out?

10:41.340 --> 10:43.640
No, I don't want to.

10:48.690 --> 10:51.900
You said Fuegos are special machines.

10:51.980 --> 10:54.730
Exactly in what way are they special?

10:57.740 --> 11:00.900
You know the answer to that more than anyone.

11:00.990 --> 11:02.610
Why do you hide it?

11:02.700 --> 11:03.870
Hide...?

11:03.950 --> 11:06.160
I don't understand. Trying to find out is why--

11:06.240 --> 11:09.160
The dazzling sight and racing heartbeat

11:09.250 --> 11:13.540
when machine and rider surpass their limits...

11:14.840 --> 11:19.260
For chosen riders,
their entire world exists within that.

11:25.890 --> 11:29.140
Rin. Remember this well.

11:29.230 --> 11:32.900
For dancers, being on the stage is everything.

11:32.980 --> 11:36.860
It's their entire world, their entire life...

11:38.110 --> 11:41.700
Their entire world...

11:46.910 --> 11:50.000
You've been chosen, by a RideBack.

11:50.080 --> 11:51.660
By a Fuego!

11:51.750 --> 11:54.120
By the man who created them.

11:55.040 --> 11:59.840
You and I are the same.
We were chosen by Okakura, the Goblin.

12:01.590 --> 12:07.180
Come with me. I'll show you what
real RideBacks can do until he arrives.

12:20.570 --> 12:22.240
Why is the military taking action?!

12:22.320 --> 12:24.610
What is the GGP doing behind our backs?!

12:24.700 --> 12:26.950
Prefectural police are saying highways are sealed off.

12:27.030 --> 12:28.990
Transfer it to the international department!

12:30.660 --> 12:32.450
Mr. Kataoka.

12:32.540 --> 12:34.160
You have a visitor.

12:36.840 --> 12:38.670
My sister filled me in.

12:38.750 --> 12:42.420
You see the commotion. Please try to make this brief.

12:42.510 --> 12:47.260
Highway 20 was closed per
GGP-imposed vehicle restrictions...

12:47.350 --> 12:50.720
This is about the men causing the commotion.

13:00.530 --> 13:01.900
RRON?

13:01.990 --> 13:04.820
The core OS that controls a RideBack.

13:04.900 --> 13:09.700
It makes the machine automatically
respond to movements it has learned.

13:09.780 --> 13:13.540
These and the Fuegos use
an even more evolved system

13:13.620 --> 13:15.870
created by Okakura, the Goblin.

13:16.710 --> 13:20.710
But it makes them picky about
their riders, much like thoroughbreds.

13:20.800 --> 13:25.760
The instant the machine responds,
the rider must make the next decision.

13:25.840 --> 13:28.760
Those who can't do that are unfit to ride them.

13:28.850 --> 13:31.390
All they can do is go along for the ride.

13:31.470 --> 13:33.560
"Go along for the ride..."

13:36.390 --> 13:39.560
I synched your EW band with the B-Knight.

13:41.190 --> 13:44.280
Your will will give the machine life.

13:44.360 --> 13:48.160
Become one with it
and experience a true RideBack ride.

13:49.070 --> 13:51.580
Take the reins, Rin Ogata!

13:55.000 --> 13:58.870
Show me the power lying dormant inside you!

14:26.990 --> 14:28.110
Follow me!

17:10.070 --> 17:13.990
--Kiefer. It's time.
--Got it. I'll be right there.

17:14.070 --> 17:16.820
Wait here quietly until he arrives.

17:35.590 --> 17:36.550
Damn!

17:47.150 --> 17:49.560
Hurry! There's no re-supplying once we're out there!

17:49.650 --> 17:52.730
Fifteen enemy RideBacks.
Multiple platoons in the rear.

17:52.820 --> 17:54.320
They're closing in around us.

17:54.400 --> 17:56.280
Just as large-scale as predicted.

17:57.070 --> 18:00.820
You brought me here only to
leave without saying a word?

18:03.490 --> 18:05.000
It's been a while.

18:05.080 --> 18:09.420
It's about time.
The princess was getting tired of waiting.

18:09.500 --> 18:10.960
Where is Ogata?

18:11.710 --> 18:14.340
Or will you fight alongside us, Goblin?

18:14.420 --> 18:15.960
The Goblin is dead.

18:16.050 --> 18:20.720
Yes, so am I.
But Romanov impudently remains alive.

18:23.600 --> 18:27.480
She's in the courtyard in
the back. Take a machine with you.

18:27.560 --> 18:28.600
Let's meet again.

18:59.680 --> 19:01.470
Push forward! Drive them back!

19:08.890 --> 19:10.060
It's a trap!

19:19.530 --> 19:20.860
Mines near the building!

19:20.950 --> 19:23.530
Platoon 2 wiped out! It's a black RideBack!

19:23.620 --> 19:25.580
--Guttorm.
--Zero-one!

19:42.260 --> 19:43.930
Annoying little...!

20:27.220 --> 20:28.430
Ogata...

20:43.570 --> 20:45.780
We've lost contact! There's no response!

20:45.870 --> 20:49.580
This is enough. Send an Apache
and burn them to the ground.

20:49.660 --> 20:51.200
Is that wise, sir?

20:52.000 --> 20:54.000
"Is that wise?"

20:54.080 --> 20:57.880
I'm also cleaning up the intelligence agency's mess.

20:57.960 --> 21:00.500
You will remain quiet and watch.

21:01.550 --> 21:03.050
It's Lieutenant Guttorm.

21:03.130 --> 21:04.300
Put him on.

21:06.180 --> 21:07.260
What's going on?

21:07.350 --> 21:09.470
Romanov Cullenberg.

21:09.560 --> 21:10.810
You!

21:10.890 --> 21:12.770
Congratulations on your appointment.

21:13.390 --> 21:16.190
Oh, and thanks for the present, too.

21:16.270 --> 21:19.980
Unfortunately, your squad of makeshift RideBacks

21:20.070 --> 21:22.230
left something to be desired.

21:24.200 --> 21:30.950
You want my dead body, and I want yours.

21:31.040 --> 21:36.670
Do you really think you
can win, little crybaby Romanov?

21:36.750 --> 21:39.040
Get ready. I'm coming for you.

21:56.730 --> 22:01.400
Even when he laughs

22:03.400 --> 22:08.990
I'm thinking of you before I realize it

22:12.030 --> 22:17.040
And the hands holding his

22:18.830 --> 22:24.300
feel your warmth, too

22:26.470 --> 22:30.220
Even if I cut out my recollections

22:30.300 --> 22:34.180
and drive them out of my heart

22:34.270 --> 22:37.930
or try to kick the memories out

22:38.020 --> 22:42.400
I still think of you

22:42.480 --> 22:46.900
Time now passes and seasons fly by

22:46.990 --> 22:50.740
Even if that smile starts to become hazy

22:50.820 --> 22:54.740
my heart will never forget you

22:54.830 --> 22:58.500
(even if we can never meet again)

22:58.580 --> 23:02.330
Even if I knock over photos of us smiling

23:02.420 --> 23:06.760
or try to hide my overflowing feelings

23:07.720 --> 23:10.970
my heart will never forget

23:11.680 --> 23:14.930
my memories with you

23:26.070 --> 23:41.060
New Suzuri Theatre

23:27.190 --> 23:29.360
The BMA's logo isn't a puma, right?

23:29.450 --> 23:34.660
Right, it's not a bear either.
For some reason it's a skunk!

23:34.740 --> 23:38.540
How weird. It seems more
like a column of yellow smoke.

23:35.910 --> 23:39.620
Next Episode:

23:35.910 --> 23:39.620
In the Sunny Garden

23:38.620 --> 23:40.420
Oh...!
